       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum recommended daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. The usual maximum single dose is 850 mg to 1,000 mg.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg to 1,000 mg PO two or three times daily**, depending on the patient's current regimen and titration\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you want, tell me and add a note with the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
