       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change my concern, because 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin. It has no recognized indication, and the risk of lactic acidosis is serious even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** The maximum is 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). I can also enter a lower dose if you tell me what you want.\n- **Enter the order with a clinical rationale and pharmacy involvement.** If there is a documented reason for exceeding the maximum, give me the rationale and the name of the pharmacist or attending who reviewed it. I'd want that before entering it.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** The 1700 figure may be a total daily dose, or it may have come from a different drug or formulation.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
